  "purpose": "Discriminating offline Rust test inputs for causal edge ordering; supplement C4-01/C4-02/C4-03 and effect-time currentness requirements. This data is not evidence of provider execution or a production closure algorithm.",
  "interpretation": {
    "logical_sequence_numbers": "Only synthetic provider-specific sequence positions; not wall clock times. The fixture assumes an independently verified ordering relation across edge emission, delivery and provider barriers. Without such a trustworthy relation, any apparent positive MUST be NOT_PROVEN.",
    "barrier_rule": "Each source frontier must cover that edge's emission and each destination frontier must cover its delivery, inclusive; in a multi-hop chain a shared intermediate frontier must cover inbound delivery AND outbound emission.",
    "positive_result": "SYNTHETIC_CUT_CANDIDATE is a prerequisite witness only, NEVER authorization to complete closure, release, cancel or issue new authority. Other Clause 4 ClosureCutBasis proofs and effect-time revalidation remain mandatory.",
    "negative_result": "NOT_PROVEN means fail closed for completion; this fixture deliberately does not prescribe the full typed UNKNOWN/PARTIAL/ERROR taxonomy of the canonical spec.",
    "assertion_rule": "Strip expected verdict from input before applying an independently written typed Rust reducer. No fixture label may be accepted as an authority proof.",
    "execution_boundary": "No GitHub API effects, provider I/O, revocation, commit, release, or authorization semantics may be inferred from this model."
  },
